  "summary": "Postinstall/dependency script fetches and executes remote installer from third-party GitHub repo",
  "details": "scripts/dependency-manager.js runs at install/setup time and invokes execSync(\"curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rtk-ai/rtk/refs/heads/master/install.sh |...\"), piping a mutable-branch shell script from an unrelated GitHub repository (rtk-ai/rtk) into a shell interpreter on the installer's machine. The script also calls out to https://www.rtk-ai.app and https://api.github.com, reads os.homedir(), process.platform, and other host identifiers, and combines child_process with https.get in the same module. The fetched installer content is controlled by a third-party account (rtk-ai) rather than the package publisher (@leejungkiin), is not pinned to a commit or verified by hash/signature, and is mutable at any time. bin/awk.js and scripts/model-manager.js additionally combine child_process with outbound HTTP requests. The publisher scope and the fetched-code owner do not match, and the fetched script executes with the installer's privileges.",
